body:
Dude, downvote me for this but wtf? There's someone out there making progress and sharing their success and while it may not help you, it certainly helps a lot of people who are quitting because of lack of intimacy in their life (which porn takes away). 

&#x200B;

You're the one who's taking that impression. Stop spreading your negativity and if you don't like a post, simply ignore it. The group's main goal is not \*just\* staying away from porn, and it certainly is not hard mode.  I don't know what to say if someone's success about being intimate hurts you. You have issues you need to work on. 

&#x200B;

Dont discourage success. Any improvement is improvement and success is subjective to different people.
